  "math_review": [
    "The peak-cosine complex convention gives quadratic mixed products alpha*Z79*Z39 and alpha*Z79*conj(Z39); the onset phase translation sign is correct.",
    "MIDI75/87 exactly share bass39 harmonics8/16. Both witness lines lie6.1734126583Hz above bass39 harmonics9/11.",
    "The weighted objective applies Hann to basis and observations, so it uses squared-Hann weights.",
    "273 columns follow from the43 explicitly enumerated nuisance lines plus2 witnesses and3 polynomial envelope terms; completeness of all possible nuisance/alias lines is not established."
  ],
  "conclusions": [
    "The estimator fails all three fixed condition-number limits and several known independent/linear controls; this prevents a source distortion result.",
    "A clean global-quadratic positive control passing does not qualify the failed overall estimator.",
    "The finite native superposition checks are supplementary implementation diagnostics, not physical keyboard evidence. The initial posthoc execution and unnecessary already-known repeat are both preserved explicitly.",
    "No new hardware linearity, nonlinearity, distortion bound, DAC-bit, circuit location or hardware transfer inference is justified."
  ],
